{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_md_itinerary_generation_algorithm", "label": "Itinerary Generation Algorithm (documented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Itinerary Generation Algorithm", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Documents the pipeline: eligibility filter (lat/lon required), optional shuffle, angle-sweep contiguous-arc day assignment, per-day trim applied after assignment to preserve spatial clusters (a global pre-trim would drop the createdAt tail), and nearest-neighbour greedy ordering within each day with short days (<=2) skipping the greedy pass."}, {"id": "claude_md_chat_side_effect_contract", "label": "Chat Side-Effect Contract (documented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Architecture > Chat Assistant", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The chat route does no side-effect work itself; it returns sideEffects[] which the client applies (search, refresh_itineraries, generate). If the generate POST throws, the client surfaces the real error as 'Generation failed: <msg>' instead of the LLM's optimistic message."}, {"id": "claude_md_drag_reanchor_pattern", "label": "Drag Re-Anchor Pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Changelog 2026-05-26", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drag uses a re-anchor pattern (lastY / currentHeight advanced only by actualDelta) so the cursor stays glued to the divider line in both directions, even after pushing past a bound. Bounds: min = default 256px, max = the inner list's natural offsetHeight."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_md_itinerary_generation_algorithm", "target": "generate_POST", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": "Archite